export const STORE_KNOWLEDGE = "# The business\nBrand: Body Café Co. Sold by Bluebell Lifecare Pvt. Ltd.\nRegistered office: Office No. 202, 2nd Floor, Primate, Opp. Mother Milk Palace, Nr. Judges Bungalows Cross Road, Bodakdev, Ahmedabad, Gujarat 380054, India.\nGSTIN 24AAOCB2181Q1Z6. FSSAI licence 10726994000121.\nSupport hours: Monday to Saturday, 10:00–18:00 IST (closed on Sundays and public holidays). First reply: Within one business day.\nWays to reach support: Contact form (Open a case here. You get a reference straight away and can follow it in your account.); Email (care@bodycafeco.com); WhatsApp (+91-9274248974); Phone (+91-9274248974). The contact form is at /contact.\nGrievance officer: Nayan Solanki, Grievance Officer · care@bodycafeco.com · +91-9274248974.\n\n# Help Centre answers (the page for each is given beside it)\n\n## Orders\nQ: Where is my order? (/help/orders/track-order)\nA: Open the order in your account. Its page shows each step and, once it ships, the courier and tracking number. Every order has a page with its status: order created, payment received, shipped and delivered. When the parcel is handed to the courier, the tracking number and courier updates appear on the same page. Ordered as a guest? The order is listed in the account area of the browser you used. Sign in with the mobile number you gave at checkout and orders placed in that browser move into your account.\nUseful pages: Your orders: /account/orders; Shipping & Delivery: /policies/shipping#tracking\nQ: I ordered without an account. How do I see my order? (/help/orders/guest-order)\nA: In the same browser, your order is listed under Account. To keep it, sign in with the mobile number you used at checkout. Signing in uses a one-time code sent to your mobile number. Orders from that browser session that used the same number join your account. We don’t show order details to anyone who can’t verify the mobile number on the order.\nUseful pages: Sign in: /sign-in?next=/account/orders\nQ: Can I cancel my order? (/help/orders/cancel-order)\nA: You can cancel from the order page until it’s dispatched. You’ll see what happens to your payment before you confirm. Open the order and choose Cancel order. If you’ve paid, the full amount is refunded. If payment is still being confirmed, check its status first. Once an order has been dispatched it can’t be cancelled. Contact us about it, or see Returns & Refunds when it arrives.\nUseful pages: Request cancellation: /account/orders; Cancellations policy: /policies/cancellation\nQ: Can I change an order after placing it? (/help/orders/change-order)\nA: Orders can’t be edited once placed. Before dispatch you can cancel and order again; for a delivery address change, contact us with the order reference. We’ll tell you whether a change is still possible. A change isn’t confirmed until we reply on your case.\nUseful pages: Contact support: /contact?topic=delivery\n\n## Delivery\nQ: Where do you deliver? (/help/delivery/delivery-areas)\nA: We deliver across India through our courier partners. Enter your pincode in your bag or at checkout to check it. If our courier partners can’t reach your pincode, we tell you before you pay. Delivery times depend on your pincode and are shown as an estimate, not a promise.\nUseful pages: Shipping & Delivery: /policies/shipping#where\nQ: How much is delivery? (/help/delivery/delivery-charges)\nA: Delivery is ₹75, free when the subtotal after discount is ₹1,499 or more. The charge is shown in your bag and at checkout before you pay, as part of a single total.\nUseful pages: Shipping & Delivery: /policies/shipping#charges\nQ: My parcel is late, lost, damaged or incomplete (/help/delivery/parcel-problem)\nA: Tell us from the order page or the contact form. Include your order reference; a photo helps with damage but isn’t required. Late or lost: we’ll check with the courier and update your case. Damaged or incomplete: we’ll arrange a remedy. You’re entitled to a refund or replacement for goods that arrive damaged, wrong or late, whatever the policy says.\nUseful pages: Report an issue: /contact?topic=delivery; Shipping & Delivery: /policies/shipping#problems\nQ: Can I change my delivery address? (/help/delivery/change-address)\nA: Before dispatch, contact us with the order reference and the new address. It isn’t changed until we confirm on your case. After dispatch the courier decides whether a change is possible. We’ll ask them for you and tell you on your case.\nUseful pages: Contact support: /contact?topic=delivery\n\n## Returns\nQ: Something is wrong with my order (/help/returns/something-wrong)\nA: Start a request from the order page: choose the item, what went wrong and whether you’d prefer a refund or replacement. Damaged, wrong, missing, faulty or expired items are always looked at. A photo can help us act faster but you don’t have to send one. If you think a product has made someone unwell or isn’t safe, report it as a product safety concern instead, so it’s handled as a priority.\nUseful pages: Your orders: /account/orders; Returns & Refunds: /policies/returns\nQ: Can I return something I no longer want? (/help/returns/change-of-mind)\nA: We don’t accept change-of-mind returns. Supplements are consumed, so for everyone’s safety we only take back items that arrived damaged, wrong, missing, faulty or expired. Report a problem within 7 days of delivery from the order page, and we’ll arrange a refund or replacement.\nUseful pages: Returns & Refunds: /policies/returns#change-of-mind\nQ: Where is my refund? (/help/returns/refund-status)\nA: The order page shows the refund status. Approved refunds are released within 7 business days. Refunds go back to the original payment method. After release, UPI refunds usually arrive within a few days; card and net-banking refunds can take up to 7 business days more, depending on your bank.\nUseful pages: Your orders: /account/orders; Returns & Refunds: /policies/returns#refunds\n\n## Payments\nQ: How can I pay? (/help/payments/payment-methods)\nA: Pay online by UPI, card, wallet or net banking, through our payment partner Razorpay. Cash on delivery isn’t available. We never see or store your card details, and we never ask for them on a support form, email or chat.\nUseful pages: Terms: /policies/terms#payment\nQ: My payment failed, or I’m not sure it went through (/help/payments/payment-unclear)\nA: Don’t pay again yet. Open the order and choose Check payment status; we’ll tell you whether the payment arrived. If money left your account but the order shows unpaid, contact us with the order reference. Don’t send card or bank details.\nUseful pages: Your orders: /account/orders; Contact support: /contact?topic=payment\nQ: How do discount codes work? (/help/payments/discounts)\nA: Enter a code in your bag under “Have a discount code?”. The discount is shown before checkout. Each offer’s conditions, such as dates or a minimum order, are shown with the offer. One code per order.\nUseful pages: Your bag: /cart\nQ: Can I get a GST invoice? (/help/payments/gst-invoice)\nA: Yes. Every order comes with a tax invoice from Bluebell Lifecare Pvt. Ltd. (GSTIN 24AAOCB2181Q1Z6). Add your GSTIN at checkout to have it on the invoice.\nUseful pages: Terms: /policies/terms#pricing\n\n## Account\nQ: How do I sign in? (/help/account/sign-in)\nA: With your mobile number and a one-time code. Checkout doesn’t need an account. We send a six-digit code by SMS. Codes last five minutes, and you can ask for a new one after a short wait.\nUseful pages: Sign in: /sign-in?next=/account\nQ: How do I change my mobile number? (/help/account/change-number)\nA: Contact us. Your orders are tied to your verified number, so we check the change before making it.\nUseful pages: Contact support: /contact?topic=account\nQ: Can I get a copy of my data or delete my account? (/help/account/your-data)\nA: Yes. Signed-in customers can download their data from Profile & security and make privacy requests there. Requests are verified by your sign-in, get a reference and appear in your account’s Support section.\nUseful pages: Privacy requests: /account/profile#privacy; Privacy: /policies/privacy#rights\nQ: How do I stop marketing messages? (/help/account/marketing)\nA: Turn them off in Preferences. Order and service messages aren’t marketing and aren’t affected.\nUseful pages: Preferences: /settings\n\n## Products\nQ: I have a question about a product (/help/products/product-question)\nA: Ask on the product page or contact us. We can’t give medical advice; please speak to a doctor about your own health. Each product page shows the serving size, directions and cautions. Always read the label on your own pack.\nUseful pages: Contact support: /contact?topic=product\nQ: I think a product is unsafe or made someone unwell (/help/products/safety)\nA: Stop using it and report it as a product safety concern. It’s handled as a priority case. If someone needs urgent care, contact a doctor or emergency services first. Tell us the product, the lot number on the pack and what happened. Keep the pack if you can.\nUseful pages: Report a safety concern: /contact?topic=safety\n\n## Lot Reports\nQ: How do I find the report for my pack? (/help/reports/find-lot)\nA: Choose your product on Lot Reports and enter the lot number on your pack. The lot number is on the bottle label, next to the manufacturing and expiry dates.\nUseful pages: Lot Reports: /reports\nQ: My lot number isn’t found (/help/reports/lot-not-found)\nA: Check for letters that look like numbers (O and 0, I and 1). If it still isn’t found, ask us from the result page; the lot is attached to your question.\nUseful pages: Lot Reports: /reports; Contact support: /contact?topic=report\n\n# Policies (Version 1.0, updated 2026-11-02)\n\n## Shipping & Delivery (/policies/shipping)\nIn short: We deliver across India through our courier partners. Delivery is ₹75 per order, and free when your subtotal after discount is ₹1,499 or more. Every order is prepaid. Cash on delivery isn’t available. If a parcel is late, lost, damaged or incomplete, tell us within 7 days of delivery and we’ll put it right.\n### Where we deliver (/policies/shipping#where)\nWe deliver to pincodes across India that our courier partners serve. Enter your pincode in your bag or at checkout; if we can’t deliver there, we tell you before you pay.\n### When orders are sent (/policies/shipping#processing)\nWe pack orders Monday to Saturday, except public holidays, and hand them to our courier partner. Your order page shows when it has shipped.\n### Delivery charges (/policies/shipping#charges)\nDelivery is ₹75 per order. It’s free when your subtotal, after any discount, is ₹1,499 or more. The delivery charge is shown in your bag and at checkout, included in a single total, before you pay.\n### Delivery estimates (/policies/shipping#estimates)\nDelivery time depends on your pincode and the courier. Any date we show is an estimate, not a promise. Remote areas can take longer.\n### Tracking (/policies/shipping#tracking)\nWhen your order ships, its page shows the courier, the tracking number and the courier’s updates.\n### Changing the delivery address (/policies/shipping#address)\nBefore dispatch, contact us with your order reference and the new address. The change is made once we confirm it on your case. After dispatch, it depends on the courier; we’ll ask them for you.\n### Failed delivery and return to us (/policies/shipping#failed)\nIf the courier can’t deliver after its attempts and the parcel comes back to us, we contact you and agree whether to send it again or refund the order.\n### Late, lost, damaged or incomplete parcels (/policies/shipping#problems)\nTell us within 7 days of delivery from the order page or the contact form, with your order reference. A photo helps with damage but isn’t required. If goods arrive damaged, wrong, defective or late, you’re entitled to a refund or replacement. Nothing in this policy limits your rights under the Consumer Protection Act, 2019 and its rules.\n### Cash on delivery (/policies/shipping#cod)\nCash on delivery isn’t available. Pay online by UPI, card, wallet or net banking.\n### Help with a delivery (/policies/shipping#help)\nUse Contact and choose “An order: delivery, tracking or address”. We reply Monday to Saturday, 10:00–18:00 IST, within one business day.\n\n## Returns & Refunds (/policies/returns)\nIn short: If something arrives damaged, wrong, missing, faulty or expired, tell us within 7 days of delivery and we’ll arrange a refund or replacement. We don’t accept change-of-mind returns: supplements are consumed, so we only take back items with a problem. Approved refunds go back to the original payment method within 7 business days. Product safety concerns are handled separately, as a priority.\n### Damaged, wrong, missing, faulty or expired items (/policies/returns#problem)\nStart a request from the order page. Choose the item, what went wrong and whether you’d prefer a refund or a replacement. We don’t refuse a refund or replacement for goods that are defective, deficient, spurious, not as described or delivered late.\n### Change of mind (/policies/returns#change-of-mind)\nWe don’t accept returns of items you no longer want. Supplements are consumed, and we can’t resell a returned pack safely. This doesn’t affect items that arrive with a problem.\n### Time limit (/policies/returns#windows)\nTell us within 7 days of delivery. If you notice a problem later, such as a fault inside a sealed pack, contact us anyway and we’ll look at it.\n### Condition of items (/policies/returns#condition)\nKeep the pack, its seal and the lot number if you can. It helps us trace the batch.\n### How to ask (/policies/returns#how)\nFrom your order page choose “Report a problem with this order”, or use Contact with your order reference. You get a case reference straight away and can follow progress in your account.\n### Photos and evidence (/policies/returns#evidence)\nA photo of the damage, the item and the lot number helps us act faster. It isn’t required, and we won’t refuse a request just because you don’t have one.\n### Sending items back (/policies/returns#collection)\nIf we need the item back, we arrange a pickup through our courier partner at no cost to you. Please don’t send anything until we’ve confirmed the pickup on your case.\n### Refunds (/policies/returns#refunds)\nRefunds go back to the original payment method. We review each request and release approved refunds within 7 business days; the order page shows the status. After release, UPI refunds usually arrive within a few days. Card and net-banking refunds can take up to 7 business days more, depending on your bank.\n### Delivery charges, discounts and part-refunds (/policies/returns#charges)\nWhen we refund part of an order, we refund what you paid for those items after any discount. If the whole order is refunded because of our mistake or a delivery problem, the delivery charge is refunded too.\n### Product safety (/policies/returns#safety)\nIf you think a product is unsafe or has made someone unwell, stop using it and report it as a product safety concern. It’s handled as a priority, separately from returns.\n### Your rights (/policies/returns#rights)\nNothing in this policy limits your rights under the Consumer Protection Act, 2019 and the Consumer Protection (E-Commerce) Rules, 2020.\n\n## Cancellations (/policies/cancellation)\nIn short: You can cancel from the order page until the order is dispatched. We don’t charge to cancel. If you’ve paid, the full amount is refunded. After dispatch an order can’t be cancelled; contact us, or use Returns & Refunds when it arrives. If we have to cancel, we’ll tell you why and refund everything you paid.\n### Before dispatch (/policies/cancellation#before)\nOpen the order and choose Cancel order. You’ll see what happens to your payment before you confirm. The cancellation is complete when the order page says Cancelled. Once an order has been handed to the courier, it can no longer be cancelled.\n### After dispatch (/policies/cancellation#after)\nA dispatched order can’t be cancelled. Contact us about it, or report a problem when it arrives.\n### Cancelling part of an order (/policies/cancellation#partial)\nPart-cancellation isn’t available. You can cancel the whole order and place a new one before dispatch.\n### Charges (/policies/cancellation#charges)\nWe don’t charge a cancellation fee.\n### Payment, discounts and refunds (/policies/cancellation#refund)\nIf you’ve paid, the full amount, including any delivery charge, is refunded to the original payment method within 7 business days. If payment is still being confirmed, check its status first; you can cancel once we know. The order page shows the refund status.\n### If we cancel (/policies/cancellation#ours)\nWe may need to cancel if an item becomes unavailable or a batch is held for a quality check. We’ll tell you why and refund the full amount paid.\n\n## Privacy (/policies/privacy)\nIn short: We use your details to take and deliver orders, run your account, answer support cases and publish reviews you submit. Marketing and optional analytics are off unless you turn them on, and you can turn them off at any time. We don’t use advertising or cross-site tracking technologies, and we don’t sell your data. Signed-in customers can download their data and make privacy requests from their account.\n### Who we are (/policies/privacy#who)\nBody Café Co. is a brand of Bluebell Lifecare Pvt. Ltd., Office No. 202, 2nd Floor, Primate, Opp. Mother Milk Palace, Nr. Judges Bungalows Cross Road, Bodakdev, Ahmedabad, Gujarat 380054, India. Our privacy contact is care@bodycafeco.com.\n### What we collect (/policies/privacy#collect)\nYour mobile number, when you sign in or check out. Your name, delivery address, optional email and optional GSTIN, when you check out or save an address. Your orders, payment status and order history. Card and bank details are handled by our payment partner, Razorpay, and never stored by us. Support cases: what you write, any photos you attach (location and camera details are removed) and our replies. Reviews and questions you submit, with any photos. Your choices: marketing and analytics preferences. A session cookie and some data saved in your browser (your bag, saved items, preferences and drafts). If you turn on analytics: the names of pages and actions you use on this site.\n### Where it comes from (/policies/privacy#sources)\nFrom you, and from your browser when you use the site. Our payment and courier partners also tell us payment and delivery status.\n### Why we use it (/policies/privacy#use)\nOrders: to take payment, pack and deliver your order, and handle cancellations, returns and refunds. Account: to verify your mobile number and keep your orders, addresses and cases together. Support: to answer and track your cases, including product safety concerns. Reviews: to check you received the product and to moderate what you post. Analytics (only if you turn it on): to understand which pages and features are used. Marketing (only if you turn it on): to tell you about new products and guides by email or WhatsApp. Legal duties: to keep records the law requires and respond to lawful requests.\n### Who we share it with (/policies/privacy#sharing)\nRazorpay, to take payments and refunds. Our courier partners, to deliver your order: your name, delivery address and mobile number. Our SMS provider, to send sign-in codes and order messages. Netlify and Supabase, which host this website and its database. Each gets only what it needs for that service. We may also share information when the law requires it, for example with tax authorities or in response to a lawful request. We don’t sell personal data.\n### Cookies and similar technologies (/policies/privacy#tracking)\nNecessary: a session cookie (bcc_session) that keeps you signed in and protects forms. It can’t be turned off. Necessary: browser storage for your bag, saved items, drafts and preferences. Optional: first-party analytics that records page and action names, only when you turn it on in Preferences. We don’t use advertising, personalisation or third-party tracking technologies.\n### How long we keep it (/policies/privacy#retention)\nOrders, invoices and payment records: 8 years, as tax and company law require. Your account, addresses and preferences: until you delete your account. Support cases: as long as needed to resolve them and handle any follow-up, then deleted or anonymised. Marketing consent: until you withdraw it, plus a record that you did. You can ask us to delete your data at any time. Records the law requires us to keep are kept for that period only.\n### Your choices and rights (/policies/privacy#rights)\nSee and download a copy of your data (Profile & security › Download my data). Correct or update your details. Ask us to delete your account and data. Withdraw a consent, such as marketing, at any time in Preferences. Nominate someone to act for you. Make a privacy complaint. Requests are made from your account, so we know they come from you. Each gets a reference you can follow.\n### How we check it’s you (/policies/privacy#verify)\nPrivacy requests need you to be signed in with the one-time code sent to your mobile number. We may ask for more information if a request concerns data we can’t link to your number.\n### Children (/policies/privacy#children)\nAnyone can browse, but only adults (18 or older) can buy. We don’t knowingly collect personal data from children.\n### Security and storage (/policies/privacy#security)\nSign-in codes are stored only in scrambled (hashed) form and expire after five minutes. Session cookies can’t be read by page scripts, forms are protected against cross-site requests, and photos are checked and stripped of location data before they’re stored. No system is perfectly secure, and we’ll tell you if a breach affects your data. Our hosting providers may store or process data outside India. Where they do, they protect it to the same standard as this policy.\n### The law we follow (/policies/privacy#law)\nToday, the Information Technology Act, 2000 and the Information Technology (Reasonable Security Practices and Procedures and Sensitive Personal Data or Information) Rules, 2011 apply. Most duties under the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 and the Digital Personal Data Protection Rules, 2025 begin on 13 May 2027, and this policy will be updated before then.\n### Privacy contact and grievances (/policies/privacy#contact)\nMake a privacy request from your account, or use Contact and choose “A privacy request”. Grievance Officer: Nayan Solanki, Grievance Officer, Bluebell Lifecare Pvt. Ltd., Office No. 202, 2nd Floor, Primate, Opp. Mother Milk Palace, Nr. Judges Bungalows Cross Road, Bodakdev, Ahmedabad, Gujarat 380054. Email care@bodycafeco.com, phone +91-9274248974 (Monday to Saturday, 10:00–18:00 IST). We acknowledge a grievance within 48 hours and resolve it within one month.\n### Changes to this policy (/policies/privacy#changes)\nWhen this policy changes in a way that matters, we’ll update the version and date at the top and tell signed-in customers.\n\n## Terms (/policies/terms)\nIn short: These terms cover your use of this website and anything you buy from Body Café Co. You must be 18 or older to buy. Our products are supplements, not medicines. Follow the label and talk to a doctor about your health. Shipping, returns and cancellation have their own policies, linked below. Your consumer rights always apply.\n### Who we are (/policies/terms#who)\nBody Café Co. is a brand of Bluebell Lifecare Pvt. Ltd., Office No. 202, 2nd Floor, Primate, Opp. Mother Milk Palace, Nr. Judges Bungalows Cross Road, Bodakdev, Ahmedabad, Gujarat 380054, India. GSTIN 24AAOCB2181Q1Z6. FSSAI Lic. No. 10726994000121.\n### What these terms cover (/policies/terms#scope)\nYour use of this website and anything you buy from it. By placing an order you agree to these terms and the policies linked below.\n### Your account (/policies/terms#account)\nYou sign in with your mobile number and a one-time code. Keep your phone and codes to yourself, and tell us if you think someone else has used your account. Checkout doesn’t require an account.\n### Product information and availability (/policies/terms#products)\nWe try to describe products accurately, using the approved label. If the label and the website differ, the label on the pack is the authority. Products are available while stock lasts; your bag tells you if stock changes before you pay.\n### Ordering (/policies/terms#ordering)\nYou must be 18 or older to buy. Placing an order is an offer to buy; it’s accepted when payment is confirmed. We may decline or cancel an order — for example, if an item becomes unavailable or a batch is held for a quality check — and we’ll refund anything you paid. Your order becomes a contract when payment is confirmed and we send your order confirmation.\n### Prices, tax and payment (/policies/terms#pricing)\nPrices are the MRP in Indian rupees, inclusive of all taxes. The total, including any delivery charge, is shown as a single figure before you pay. Every order comes with a tax invoice from Bluebell Lifecare Pvt. Ltd. (GSTIN 24AAOCB2181Q1Z6); add your GSTIN at checkout to have it on the invoice. Payment is taken by our payment partner, Razorpay; we don’t store card details. Offers and discount codes come with their own conditions, shown with the offer.\n### Payment methods (/policies/terms#payment)\nPay online by UPI, card, wallet or net banking. Every order is prepaid; cash on delivery isn’t available.\n### Shipping, returns and cancellations (/policies/terms#policies)\nSee Shipping & Delivery, Returns & Refunds and Cancellations. They form part of these terms.\n### Using our products (/policies/terms#use)\nOur products are food supplements, not medicines, and are not intended to diagnose, treat, cure or prevent any disease. Follow the directions and cautions on the label. Don’t exceed the recommended daily usage. If you’re pregnant, breastfeeding, taking medication, have a medical condition, or are buying for someone under 18, speak to a doctor first. Keep out of reach of children.\n### Reviews and what you submit (/policies/terms#reviews)\nReviews come from signed-in customers whose order was delivered, and every review is moderated before it appears, whatever its rating. Don’t post anything unlawful, misleading, or that includes someone else’s personal details. You allow us to display what you submit on this site; you can ask us to remove it.\n### Our content (/policies/terms#ip)\nThe Body Café Co. name, logo, designs, text and images belong to us or our licensors. You may share links to the site but not copy its content for commercial use.\n### Our responsibility to you (/policies/terms#liability)\nWe’re responsible for providing products as described and for the remedies the law gives you. Nothing in these terms limits liability that can’t be limited by law, including your rights under the Consumer Protection Act, 2019.\n### Complaints and disputes (/policies/terms#complaints)\nContact us first; you get a case reference. If you’re not satisfied, ask for it to go to our Grievance Officer: Nayan Solanki, Grievance Officer, Bluebell Lifecare Pvt. Ltd., Office No. 202, 2nd Floor, Primate, Opp. Mother Milk Palace, Nr. Judges Bungalows Cross Road, Bodakdev, Ahmedabad, Gujarat 380054. Email care@bodycafeco.com, phone +91-9274248974 (Monday to Saturday, 10:00–18:00 IST). We acknowledge a grievance within 48 hours and resolve it within one month. You can also contact the National Consumer Helpline (1915 or 1800-11-4000, consumerhelpline.gov.in) or approach a consumer commission. Governing law: India. Courts at Ahmedabad, Gujarat have jurisdiction; this doesn’t affect your right to bring a consumer complaint where the law allows.\n### Changes to these terms (/policies/terms#changes)\nThe version and date at the top show which terms apply. Orders are governed by the terms in force when you placed them.";
